    "notes": "1. Scale: Values are in millions (1E6) as indicated in the statement header.\n2. Total Revenue: Composed of 'Product' and 'Service and other' line items.\n3. Total Operating Cost: Includes all costs and expenses deducted from revenue to arrive at Operating Income. This comprises 'Total cost of revenue' (split into Product and Service and other) and the three operating expense categories: Research and development, Sales and marketing, and General and administrative.\n4. Taxes: 'Provision for income taxes' is the tax assessed on income.\n5. Interest Expenses: 'Interest expense' is taken from the supplementary breakdown of 'Other income (expense), net'. The value is reported as a positive number as it is an expense that reduces income.\n6. Other items in 'Other income (expense), net' (e.g., interest income, investment gains/losses, foreign currency remeasurements) are not part of the requested normalized fields and are therefore excluded.\n7. The segment information and detailed revenue breakdowns are supplementary and not required for the core income statement fields requested.",
